[Habits]
  Home -> A
  Bed -> B

[Life]
  Games -> G
  Computers -> C

#[Time::time]::MMDDYY
  08:17:2025
  08:17:2025

#[Rating]
#[Flags::colored]::ORDER
  (A) - Normal
  (B) - Very Good

  (G) - Good
  (C) - Very Good

#[Type::Icons]

explanation:
  - the names captalized between the curly brackets are the name of the columns.

  - time is all lowercase because it's a default type.
  - MMDDYY is the format applied in the column.
  
  - Rating is also a default type that have formats like ORDER.
  - ORDER default format of Rating that rates based in order of (a ordem em que os valores aparecem).
  - Rating is not lower case being a default type like time and colored because is called in a diffrent way, i way that allows bind types

  - colored will apply a color to the values following some patter or directly.
  - in this case the pattern is determined by Rating::ORDER.

  - when we have something like Type::(some name) is a definition of a type just like the default Types.
